-- title:
--   Degree-one primes over ℓ count cosets fixed by D_{Q_0}
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a number field that is Galois over $\mathbb{Q}$, write $G = L \simeq_{\mathbb{Q}} L$ for its automorphism group, let $H$ be a subgroup of $G$ and $E$ an intermediate field of $L/\mathbb{Q}$ such that $H$ is the Galois group of $L$ over $E$ (the instance `IsGaloisGroup H E L`). Let $\ell$ be a prime number and let $Q_0$ be a prime ideal of $\mathcal{O}_L$ lying over the ideal of $\mathbb{Z}$ generated by $\ell$, that is, over $\ell\mathbb{Z}$, and assume that the inertia subgroup of $Q_0$ in $G$ is trivial. Then the number of prime ideals $\mathfrak{q}$ of $\mathcal{O}_E$ lying over $\ell\mathbb{Z}$ whose residue ring $\mathcal{O}_E/\mathfrak{q}$ has exactly $\ell$ elements (i.e. the degree-one primes of $E$ above $\ell$) equals the number of cosets $x \in G/H$ with $d \cdot x = x$ for every $d$ in the stabiliser of $Q_0$ under the action of $G$ on ideals of $\mathcal{O}_L$, both counts being taken as `Set.ncard`.
--
--   This is the decomposition-group form of the Frobenius counting identity: degree-one primes of the subfield $E = L^H$ above an unramified rational prime $\ell$ correspond to the cosets in $G/H$ fixed by the decomposition group $D_{Q_0} = \mathrm{Stab}_G(Q_0)$. It is used to obtain the Frobenius form of the count, [`FrobeniusDensity.ncard_degreeOne_primesOver_eq_ncard_frobFixed`](thm.html#FrobeniusDensity.ncard_degreeOne_primesOver_eq_ncard_frobFixed), via the identification of $D_{Q_0}$ with the cyclic group generated by the arithmetic Frobenius at $Q_0$, which is the shape needed for the Chebotarev-type density arguments supplying auxiliary Taylor–Wiles primes.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_FrobeniusDensity_ncard_degreeOne_primesOver_under.lean

import Definitions.Def_TaylorWiles_Primes
